# Satisfying runtime contract (port of contracts-runtime-violation.test.ts,
# the positive arm): compile + run must succeed (rc=0) and the program must
# actually RUN — the kept "d = 5" line is the program output, so a binary
# that never executed cannot pass. Build chatter differs between compilers,
# hence the keep filter.
stdout_keep=^d = 
timeout=300
